Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.89,0:00:09.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.60,0:00:13.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm wondering if\Neveryone else is safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.85,0:00:17.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are a lot of people in the east\Nwho have the same skin color as you,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.82,0:00:19.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so I think they were\Nable to slip in.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.61,0:00:23.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, you are seen as the\Ninstigator of the rebellion in Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.49,0:00:31.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That looks like the temple of the Lord Leto, back in Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.50,0:00:34.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is from an even older religion.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.87,0:00:37.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's no longer being\Npracticed now, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.66,0:01:09.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. They only recognized one god
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.83,0:01:14.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and considered all other gods\Nto be heathen.\NIt's said they had\Na lot of believers.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.21,0:01:19.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Many people died because of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.75,0:01:20.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A great many.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.42,0:01:22.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's awful.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.92,0:01:25.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Religions exist to save people.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.59,0:01:27.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,People cannot become gods, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.76,0:01:32.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There, there. It's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.27,0:01:37.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why did you let\Nthose two get away?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.10,0:01:43.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was {\i1}your{\i0} duty to eliminate the brothers, wasn't it, Sloth?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.11,0:01:43.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You too, Wrath.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.36,0:01:45.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll get them next time.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.61,0:01:49.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You defied that\Ncertain someone's word.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.07,0:01:53.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sloth, don't you want\Nto become human?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.04,0:01:55.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.71,0:01:59.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After all, I was born\Nto become human.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.33,0:02:02.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't have any other goal.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.80,0:02:10.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.48,0:02:25.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.53,0:02:31.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who obtain it are set free from the Law of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.16,0:02:35.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is no need to pay a price\Nin order to obtain something, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.04,0:02:40.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We sought it and found it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.15,0:04:31.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why did you run off on your own\Nwithout coming to me for protection?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.16,0:04:43.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elric brothers, what happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.21,0:04:47.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,King Bradley is...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.50,0:04:49.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,a homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.92,0:04:58.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By homunculus, you mean those...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.30,0:04:58.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,man-made people, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.22,0:04:59.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.64,0:05:03.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They are covertly\Nmanipulating this country\Nin order to get a\NPhilosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.81,0:05:06.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.48,0:05:10.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer did not know what was taking place at the 5th Laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.48,0:05:13.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He also lamented the corruption within the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.40,0:05:15.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I saw it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.70,0:05:18.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer had the\Nmark of the Uroboros!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.99,0:05:21.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was the one homunculus who can change his shape.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.95,0:05:24.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer's secretary is also a homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.08,0:05:28.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet, she's an alien...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.21,0:05:32.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Supposing that the Führer and\NSecretary Douglas are homunculi,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.46,0:05:33.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,what is their objective?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.96,0:05:35.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why have they\Ninfiltrated the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.51,0:05:43.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will send them back to Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.72,0:05:47.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll come up with an\Nappropriate reason\Nfor them not to return to Central for a little while.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.06,0:05:49.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You do that. As for us...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.81,0:05:51.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going to Resembool, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.44,0:05:57.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gentlemen, rejoice!\NOur duties are at an end!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.11,0:05:59.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major, what were you \Njust talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.95,0:06:03.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Were you listening to the melody\Nbeing played by this body of mine?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.49,0:06:05.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, not that...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.66,0:06:07.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Listen closely!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.62,0:06:09.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hear that? Hear that?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.84,0:06:17.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um...\NHow is Lieutenant Havoc?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.01,0:06:20.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's okay. He and Fuery\Nwere sent back ahead of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.60,0:06:22.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.26,0:06:24.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry about all that.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.10,0:06:29.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed, your silver watch...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.44,0:06:32.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.61,0:06:35.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't be\Na State Alchemist anymore,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.53,0:06:37.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,if what you said earlier is true.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.53,0:06:39.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, it's not that.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.65,0:06:41.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I mean, it was taken\Nfrom me by Archer.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.74,0:06:44.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Didn't Al-kun\Ngive it back to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.50,0:06:49.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-I'm sorry! Brother,\NI don't have it anymore!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.58,0:06:50.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You lost it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.96,0:06:52.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,N-No!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.17,0:06:53.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kimbly threw it at Scar-san,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.96,0:06:56.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and all the red stones inside it\Ncame spilling out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.55,0:06:58.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then they were absorbed into Scar-san's arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.92,0:07:02.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why were there red stones inside my silver watch?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.43,0:07:03.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That miserable Archer.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.85,0:07:06.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He used that trick again,\Ncalling them transmutation amplifiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.72,0:07:07.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.56,0:07:12.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Previously, in Ishbal, Brig. Gen. Grand\Nsupplied us with red stones.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.11,0:07:15.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on, Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.11,0:07:18.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then you knew that the military \Nwas making Philosopher's Stones?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.74,0:07:20.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet, you didn't\Nsay anything to me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.78,0:07:23.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When Marcoh deserted,\NI thought it had been discontinued.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.24,0:07:26.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Besides, it's not as though I knew that people were used as ingredients.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.24,0:07:28.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't trust you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.41,0:07:29.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.54,0:07:31.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You couldn't forget about those red stones,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.29,0:07:33.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so you tried to send us out to find them!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.97,0:07:33.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop it, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.58,0:07:34.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Enough already!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.54,0:07:35.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.80,0:07:42.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.26,0:07:45.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al can't go in the water!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.88,0:07:45.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al! Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.10,0:07:46.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.14,0:07:49.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.74,0:08:05.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! I can swim!\NI can swim, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.78,0:08:07.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.96,0:08:19.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your bloodseal washes off if you're submerged in water, doesn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.09,0:08:21.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.76,0:08:23.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Looks like I don't\Nhave to worry about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.80,0:08:27.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if that's because I really\Nhave become a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.76,0:08:32.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,O-Okay, I get it! Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.89,0:08:34.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What did you just...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.64,0:08:36.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's nothing...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.15,0:08:38.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What...\Ndid you just say about\Nthe Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.57,0:08:41.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing at all, nothing at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.82,0:08:42.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, let's get going!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.11,0:08:45.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother! Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.79,0:08:53.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Looks like the military\Nhasn't arrived yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.83,0:08:57.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.29,0:08:58.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sergeant Brosh?\NHe's in pursuit?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.21,0:09:01.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,N-No, that's not it. Not him.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.63,0:09:04.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brosh-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.93,0:09:07.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's wrong, exactly?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.64,0:09:10.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Lieutenant Ross is...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.60,0:09:11.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Ross is...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.10,0:09:17.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Your hair is as deep black\Nas the feathers
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.31,0:09:21.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,of the great eagles I saw, so long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.94,0:09:27.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I never thought I would see anything so beautiful again.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.32,0:09:29.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your flattery is far too kind.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.33,0:09:34.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Lieutenant, single-minded to her work, has gone absolutely sentimental over him!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.25,0:09:35.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of all the things it could have been...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.87,0:09:37.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.67,0:09:41.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But who is she with, Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.34,0:09:43.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.05,0:09:48.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you flirting with her for?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.51,0:09:49.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.89,0:09:55.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't come home for umpteen years,\Nand {\i1}this{\i0} is how I find you?!\NYou rotten old man!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.39,0:09:58.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.56,0:10:03.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah... Just like in the picture...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.53,0:10:04.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.82,0:10:08.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's Dad! It's Dad!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.79,0:10:26.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, you probably don't know who I am in this form,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.46,0:10:27.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I'm...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.67,0:10:30.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alphonse! You've gotten bigger, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.18,0:10:33.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know who I am?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.60,0:10:36.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.06,0:10:40.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You still hate milk, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.44,0:10:44.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you saying hasn't grown one bit since he was a baby?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.03,0:10:46.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not what he said.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.99,0:10:50.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure, Edward-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.32,0:10:51.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure, I'm sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.70,0:10:53.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't get me wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.41,0:10:56.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was just listening to\Nthe stories of his travels.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.95,0:10:58.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, you did look like you were enjoying it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.58,0:11:02.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, he is such a gentleman.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.17,0:11:06.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With a whiff of his cologne\Nsubtly carrying on the breeze,\Nhe's not the type of man we get in the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.42,0:11:09.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cologne doesn't suit me, anyhow...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.92,0:11:12.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you acting so coy?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.01,0:11:16.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cologne, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.64,0:11:18.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hated that about him, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.85,0:11:23.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He left home\Nsoon after Al was born.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.86,0:11:29.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom always said he was off studying alchemy,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.40,0:11:31.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but he never once\Neven sent us a letter.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.07,0:11:37.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet, the scent of that cologne he wore \Nalways permeated the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.08,0:11:42.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Earlier, when I saw Lyra in Liore,\Nshe was wearing perfume that had the same scent.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.96,0:11:44.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You saw Lyra-san?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.63,0:11:47.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then she must have safely\Ngotten away from Dante-san's place!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.42,0:11:49.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a moment, if you please.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.84,0:11:54.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This Lyra-san—what kind of\Nrelationship do you two have?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.28,0:11:56.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.30,0:11:58.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Winry-san, what are you...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.55,0:11:58.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you holding that wrench?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.85,0:12:00.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.65,0:12:12.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer is married,\Nand he also has children.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.82,0:12:16.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Above all else, I've seen pictures of him when he was younger.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.62,0:12:22.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Homunculi do not take on the form of humans when they are born.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.50,0:12:28.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When they are given red stones as a source of nourishment,\Nthey get their own unique powers, as well as their form.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.00,0:12:32.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They use people's lives as food?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.84,0:12:41.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They can probably alter their appearance \Nlittle by little, to make it look like they are aging.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.97,0:12:42.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His children could be adopted.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.72,0:12:42.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.60,0:12:45.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,whatever the case,\Nhe's a homunculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.02,0:12:48.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.98,0:12:52.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You said they were making red stones\Nin the 5th Laboratory, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.36,0:12:56.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Homunculi cannot use alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.87,0:12:59.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yet how is it that they can\Nteach others how to make them?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.79,0:13:04.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean, there's someone who raises them and controls them?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.46,0:13:06.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.50,0:13:10.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,even though they are homunculi,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.17,0:13:14.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the country is managing\Nto get on all right,\Nand the military is functioning.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.72,0:13:16.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We need not concern\Nourselves with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.80,0:13:22.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why is it that the homunculi can't use alchemy?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.60,0:13:26.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Because they come from\Nthe other side of the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.35,0:13:31.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But let's not talk about that. Tell me all about Trisha,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.73,0:13:35.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,as well as everything you guys have been struggling through.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.95,0:13:37.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.57,0:13:40.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can tell just by looking\Nat your body. You guys—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.45,0:13:42.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There isn't anything to talk about.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.12,0:13:48.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our alchemy failed, and we lost our arms, legs, and bodies.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.00,0:13:50.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.09,0:13:53.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward, alchemy is not something—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.17,0:13:55.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shut up!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.09,0:13:57.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you come home now and try to put on a fatherly face!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.59,0:13:59.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom waited for you\Nthat whole time!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.05,0:14:02.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, get in here!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.22,0:14:03.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.85,0:14:07.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, I'm sleeping with Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.64,0:14:08.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.85,0:14:10.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go, Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.87,0:14:24.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wonder if I can get my body back\Nwith the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.45,0:14:30.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You could attach your soul to someone else's body with the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.79,0:14:32.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone else's body?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.88,0:14:33.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not what I meant. I...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.88,0:14:39.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your own body was lost in an equivalent exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.84,0:14:43.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You must have given up your body as the cost of obtaining something else.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.14,0:14:45.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something else?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.93,0:14:49.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you return all of that,\Nit will come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.65,0:14:53.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So then, if we can defeat that homunculus...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.61,0:14:58.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing, nothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.36,0:15:00.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're amazing, Dad!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.15,0:15:02.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know what?\NThere's something\NI want to ask you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.82,0:15:03.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.76,0:15:22.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.72,0:15:27.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I'd known this, I would have\Nbeat him up even more yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.06,0:15:30.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop joking around, and hurry\Nand come look for him with me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.89,0:15:33.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I bet he's just gone off on\Nsome other journey again.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.94,0:15:35.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fine, then I'll go by myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.69,0:15:36.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.94,0:15:39.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't leave here\Nfor a little while.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.16,0:15:44.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We just got word from Warrant Officer Falman, who was waiting at the train station.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.37,0:15:47.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The search party has arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.54,0:15:49.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going to go over there and send them back.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.58,0:15:52.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You sure you want to be harboring wanted men?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.87,0:15:55.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not as though I believe every aspect of your story.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.17,0:16:00.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I plan on ascertaining the truth\Nabout the Führer in my own way.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.42,0:16:04.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And if you find out\Nthat it {\i1}is{\i0} true?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.96,0:16:35.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now then...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.63,0:16:39.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well now, how about you go down\Ninto the underground cellar for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.09,0:16:42.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, that's okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.84,0:16:43.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.93,0:16:48.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where could Dad have gone?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.22,0:16:49.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You be quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.81,0:16:51.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,More importantly,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.22,0:16:54.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,how does the Colonel intend to\Nfind out who the Führer really is?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.44,0:17:01.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,His secretary could only have been around for about four years, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.28,0:17:02.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.19,0:17:04.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you mean Juliet Douglas,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.11,0:17:06.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,she's supposed to have been in the military\Nfor at least fourteen years.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.49,0:17:09.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no way that could be true.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.41,0:17:14.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure of it. After all, she was \Nthe cause of the Ishbalan Civil War.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.29,0:17:17.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, you mean when that soldier accidentally shot a civilian?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.42,0:17:20.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was a lie.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.67,0:17:25.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The cause of the outbreak of the war in Ishbal\Nwas manufactured by\Na secret military squad.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.98,0:17:38.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They couldn't have...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.73,0:17:42.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's it!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.86,0:17:44.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ishbal was also used for a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.90,0:17:48.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they could drive\Nthe Ishbalans to war...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.91,0:17:53.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...then maybe there was someone\Nwho would make a Philosopher's Stone\Nusing the Grand Art.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.37,0:17:54.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Would they go that far?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.96,0:17:59.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The homunculi were behind it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.92,0:18:04.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's it. And Hughes-san\Nmust have realized that much
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.63,0:18:06.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and was killed for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.15,0:18:12.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, you bastard!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.15,0:18:12.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jerk us around, will you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.19,0:18:12.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on, Ed!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.19,0:18:12.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.22,0:18:13.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's Lt. Col. Hughes!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.43,0:18:15.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was right after\Nwe left Central, wasn't it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.85,0:18:18.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The bastard!\NAnd yet, he kept us in the dark!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.35,0:18:20.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did you know about this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.15,0:18:24.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry. I just found out\Nabout it myself not long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.11,0:18:27.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In any case,\Nplease go back inside!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.24,0:18:30.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've got to be joking!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.32,0:18:33.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If Lt. Col. Hughes was killed,\Nthen it was our fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.91,0:18:35.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And yet, he didn't even...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.00,0:18:38.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.42,0:18:42.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not as though he didn't tell you\Njust to be mean, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.42,0:18:47.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard about this man Hughes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.42,0:18:49.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I understand he was good to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.80,0:18:54.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But Mustang-san doesn't want you \Nto be thinking about revenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.39,0:19:01.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe he was trying to say that you had \Nsomething more important to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.65,0:19:04.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.94,0:19:08.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've had it all wrong\Nthis whole time.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.65,0:19:13.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought the Colonel didn't care what had happened to Brigadier General Hughes.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.28,0:19:16.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But maybe...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.50,0:19:20.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll become distinguished...\Nthe most important in the country...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.25,0:19:23.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was Mustang's\Npromise to him, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.04,0:19:25.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to do that,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.75,0:19:29.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he sought for ways to get promoted, rather than dwell on personal feelings such as revenge.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.63,0:19:32.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Colonel sure is an adult, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.64,0:19:34.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can that be?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.43,0:19:37.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone dear to him was killed, and he knows who the culprit is.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.06,0:19:41.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yet there's something even more important to him than avenging his friend's death.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.44,0:19:44.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that the way that adults act?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.44,0:19:48.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You became a dog of the military\Nin order to achieve your goal, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.69,0:19:53.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That bastard.\NI really do hate him.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.07,0:19:56.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone's coming!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.24,0:19:58.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't be ridiculous.\NThis place is—
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.17,0:20:07.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.88,0:20:12.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How good of you to come.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.47,0:20:14.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, the master is out.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.68,0:20:19.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that the body of\Nthe girl named Lyra?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.06,0:20:23.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well perceived,\NHohenheim of Light.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.69,0:20:27.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure enough, you were unable to forget me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.65,0:20:30.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard her name\Nfrom my sons.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.36,0:20:32.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But even if I hadn't,\NI would've known right away
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.36,0:20:35.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,from the scent of\Nyour perfume.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.28,0:20:39.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have you come here to\Nhelp me out, or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.70,0:20:42.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, quite the opposite, Dante.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.66,0:20:44.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gluttony!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.04,0:20:47.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll eat you!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.05,0:20:54.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm scared!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.63,0:20:56.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This one doesn't use a\Ntransmutation circle either.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.05,0:20:59.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's nothing to be\Nafraid of, Gluttony.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.60,0:21:02.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He has lived far too long\Nin that body.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.73,0:21:04.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He must be near its limit.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.03,0:21:14.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am near my limit, it's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.99,0:21:17.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But the same thing\Ngoes for you too.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.62,0:21:26.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if you can hide your\Ndecaying body with clothing,\Nyou cannot disguise the smell.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.75,0:21:29.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hohenheim...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.59,0:21:30.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dante,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.71,0:21:34.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,do not mislead\Nmy sons any further.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.51,0:21:35.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you will promise me that,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.47,0:21:39.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will tell you the reason why\Nyour body has started to decay.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.43,0:21:47.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It looks like they successfully turned the military away.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.06,0:21:49.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I guess so.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.81,0:21:51.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Where's Ed?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.19,0:21:55.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said there was something he had to do alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.08,0:22:02.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Forgive me...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.16,0:22:06.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Forgive me, Mom...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.71,0:23:40.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.55,0:23:44.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 45: "A Rotted Heart"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.76,0:23:47.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al,\NI'm going to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.31,0:23:50.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't have to do\Nanything more now.
